IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc15-venue.l4 -- sections 478 to 481.3 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XIV, Jurisdiction, "Special Jurisdiction", continued):
-- in which province an offence may be tried (s 478), pleading guilty in the province where the accused is (ss 478(3), 479), unorganized territory (s 480),
-- offences not in a province (s 481), in Canadian waters (s 481.1), outside Canada (s 481.2) and the appearance of the accused (s 481.3).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Imports the core only (`ccc-core`).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: see the head of ccc15-general.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc15)"):
-- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE.

§ `Section 478 -- Offence committed entirely in one province`

-- (1) is titled as the bar: JUST TRUE means the court in a province shall not try the offence. "Subject to this Act": an exception elsewhere in the Act (s 478(2), (3), 479 to 481.2 in this range,
-- and others) displaces the bar, which the text itself says ("Subject to this Act"): JUST FALSE (fork: subject-to). The answer of those provisions is an input.
-- A "province" is not a territory: Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut are in the core's Province or territory but are not provinces.
-- src:8635 | Offence committed entirely in one province
-- src:8636 | 478 (1) Subject to this Act, a court in a province shall not try an offence committed entirely in another province.
@ref s 478(1) (src:8635-8636)
GIVEN `the province or territory in which the court is` IS A `Province or territory`
      `the province or territory in which the offence was committed entirely` IS A MAYBE `Province or territory`
      `another provision of this Act displaces the subsection, by the provisions that give the exceptions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a territory` `the province or territory in which the court is` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a court in a province" (a territory is not a province: fork: territories)
        IF NOT `the offence was committed entirely in a province` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence committed entirely in another province"
        IF `the offence was committed entirely in the province of the court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence committed entirely in another province"
        IF `another provision of this Act displaces the subsection, by the provisions that give the exceptions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to this Act" (an exception that is met: fork: subject-to)
        IF `another provision of this Act displaces the subsection, by the provisions that give the exceptions` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether another provision of this Act displaces the subsection is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `a territory` place MEANS place EQUALS Yukon OR place EQUALS `Northwest Territories` OR place EQUALS Nunavut
        `the offence was committed entirely in a province` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the province or territory in which the offence was committed entirely`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST place THEN NOT (`a territory` place)
        `the offence was committed entirely in the province of the court` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the province or territory in which the offence was committed entirely`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST place THEN place EQUALS `the province or territory in which the court is`

-- (2) Exception: a proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged with the publication of a defamatory libel in a newspaper (or conspiracy to) is dealt with in the province where
-- the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed. The question: is the province in which the person is dealt with one the text allows? "Or": either of the two provinces.
-- src:8637 | Exception
-- src:8638 | (2) Every proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged with the publication of a defamatory libel in a newspaper or with conspiracy to publish a defamatory libel in a newspaper shall be dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where he resides or in which the newspaper is printed.
@ref s 478(2) (src:8637-8638)
GIVEN `the person is a proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged with the publication of a defamatory libel in a newspaper or with conspiracy to publish a defamatory libel in a newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication is a newspaper, by s 478(5) newspaper` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the province in which the person resides` IS A `Province or territory`
      `the province in which the newspaper is printed` IS A `Province or territory`
      `the province in which the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished` IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged with the publication of a defamatory libel in a newspaper or with conspiracy to publish a defamatory libel in a newspaper` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged with the publication of a defamatory libel in a newspaper or with conspiracy to publish a defamatory libel in a newspaper"
        IF `the publication is a newspaper, by s 478(5) newspaper` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the publication is a newspaper is for section 297, through section 478(5), and is not determined
        IF `the publication is a newspaper, by s 478(5) newspaper` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a newspaper"
        IF `the province in which the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished` EQUALS `the province in which the person resides` OR `the province in which the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished` EQUALS `the province in which the newspaper is printed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where he resides or in which the newspaper is printed" (a "shall" not met: fork: bare-must)

-- (3) An accused charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province in which the accused is may, if the offence is not mentioned in section 469 and the
-- appropriate Attorney General consents, appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is.
-- "Mentioned in section 469" is the answer of `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469`: an input.
-- src:8639 | Idem
-- src:8640 | (3) An accused who is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province in which the accused is may, if the offence is not an offence mentioned in section 469 and
-- src:8641 | (a) in the case of proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government, if the Attorney General of Canada consents, or
-- src:8642 | (b) in any other case, if the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents,
-- src:8643 | appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is, and where the accused consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty to that offence, the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law, but where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty, the accused shall, if the accused was in custody prior to appearance, be returned to custody and shall be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 478(3) (src:8639-8643)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province in which the accused is` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence mentioned in section 469, by s 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and are conducted by or on behalf of that Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province in which the accused is` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province in which the accused is"
        IF `the offence is an offence mentioned in section 469, by s 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is mentioned in section 469 is not determined
        IF `the offence is an offence mentioned in section 469, by s 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the offence is not an offence mentioned in section 469" (an "if" on a power: fork: if-on-power)
        IF `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and are conducted by or on behalf of that Government`
            THEN IF `the Attorney General of Canada consents`
                 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
                 ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Attorney General of Canada consents" (an "if" on a power: fork: if-on-power)
        OTHERWISE
            IF `the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents`
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents" (an "if" on a power: fork: if-on-power)

-- "Where the accused consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty ..., the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law."
-- A "shall" whose "where" is unmet: the duty does not arise (JUST FALSE: fork: bare-must). The answer of `s 478(3) the accused may appear ...` is an input.
@ref s 478(3) (src:8639-8643)
GIVEN `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478(3) the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused may appear under the subsection is not determined
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is"
        IF NOT (`the accused consents to plead guilty` AND `the accused pleads guilty`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty to that offence" (a failed "where" on a duty: fork: bare-must)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "But where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty, the accused shall, if the accused was in custody prior to appearance, be returned to custody and shall be dealt with according to law."
-- Two duties: to be returned to custody (if in custody before the appearance), and to be dealt with according to law (whether or not in custody).
@ref s 478(3) (src:8639-8643)
GIVEN `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was in custody prior to appearance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478(3) the accused shall be returned to custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused may appear under the subsection is not determined
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is"
        IF `the accused consents to plead guilty` OR `the accused pleads guilty` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty" (a failed "where" on a duty: fork: bare-must)
        IF NOT `the accused was in custody prior to appearance` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused was in custody prior to appearance" (an "if" on a duty: fork: bare-must)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 478(3) (src:8639-8643)
GIVEN `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478(3) the accused shall be dealt with according to law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused may appear under the subsection is not determined
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 478(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is"
        IF `the accused consents to plead guilty` OR `the accused pleads guilty` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty" (a failed "where" on a duty: fork: bare-must)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4) The accused described in subsection (3) who desires to plead guilty is deemed simply to stand charged of the offence, even if ordered to stand trial or indicted: that is the effect of "Notwithstanding that",
-- so neither fact is an input.
-- src:8644 | Where accused ordered to stand trial
-- src:8645 | (4) Notwithstanding that an accused described in subsection (3) has been ordered to stand trial or that an indictment has been preferred against the accused in respect of the offence to which he desires to plead guilty, the accused shall be deemed simply to stand charged of that offence without a preliminary inquiry having been conducted or an indictment having been preferred with respect thereto.
@ref s 478(4) (src:8644-8645)
GIVEN `the accused is an accused described in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused desires to plead guilty to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478(4) the accused is deemed simply to stand charged of the offence without a preliminary inquiry having been conducted or an indictment having been preferred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is an accused described in subsection (3)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused described in subsection (3)"
        IF NOT `the accused desires to plead guilty to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of the offence to which he desires to plead guilty"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (5) newspaper has the same meaning as in section 297: an answer taken from section 297 (ccc10), carried through, and scoped by "In this section".
-- Section 478(2) reads it. The provision in which the word is used must be section 478.
-- src:8646 | Definition of newspaper
-- src:8647 | (5) In this section, newspaper has the same meaning as in section 297.
@ref s 478(5) (src:8646-8647)
GIVEN `the provision in which the word newspaper is used` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 478(5) newspaper` MEANS
    IF `the provision in which the word newspaper is used`'s `section` EQUALS 478
    THEN `s 297 the publication is a newspaper`   -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING exactly as section 297 answers
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section"

§ `Section 479 -- Offence outstanding in same province`

-- 479 is section 478(3) for an offence alleged to have been committed in the province in which the accused is: with the consent of the appropriate Attorney General, the accused appears before a court or judge
-- that would have had jurisdiction if the offence had been committed in the place where the accused is, and pleads guilty or does not.
-- src:8648 | Offence outstanding in same province
-- src:8649 | 479 Where an accused is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in the province in which he is, he may, if the offence is not an offence mentioned in section 469 and
-- src:8650 | (a) in the case of proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government, the Attorney General of Canada consents, or
-- src:8651 | (b) in any other case, the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents,
-- src:8652 | appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is, and where the accused consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty to that offence, the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law, but where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty, the accused shall, if the accused was in custody prior to appearance, be returned to custody and shall be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 479 (src:8648-8652)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in the province in which the accused is` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence mentioned in section 469, by s 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and are conducted by or on behalf of that Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of Canada consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in the province in which the accused is` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in the province in which he is" (a failed "where" on a power: fork: where-on-power)
        IF `the offence is an offence mentioned in section 469, by s 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is mentioned in section 469 is not determined
        IF `the offence is an offence mentioned in section 469, by s 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the offence is not an offence mentioned in section 469" (an "if" on a power: fork: if-on-power)
        IF `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and are conducted by or on behalf of that Government`
            THEN IF `the Attorney General of Canada consents`
                 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
                 ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Attorney General of Canada consents" (an "if" on a power: fork: if-on-power)
        OTHERWISE
            IF `the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents`
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents" (an "if" on a power: fork: if-on-power)

@ref s 479 (src:8648-8652)
GIVEN `the accused may appear, by s 479` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479 the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 479` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused may appear under the section is not determined
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 479` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is"
        IF NOT (`the accused consents to plead guilty` AND `the accused pleads guilty`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty to that offence" (a failed "where" on a duty: fork: bare-must)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 479 (src:8648-8652)
