      `the accused consents to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was in custody prior to appearance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 479 the accused shall be returned to custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 479` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused may appear under the section is not determined
        IF `the accused may appear, by s 479` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is"
        IF `the accused consents to plead guilty` OR `the accused pleads guilty` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty" (a failed "where" on a duty: fork: bare-must)
        IF NOT `the accused was in custody prior to appearance` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused was in custody prior to appearance" (an "if" on a duty: fork: bare-must)
