        IF `the accused may appear, by s 479` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is"
        IF `the accused consents to plead guilty` OR `the accused pleads guilty` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty" (a failed "where" on a duty: fork: bare-must)
