§ `Section 480 -- Offence in unorganized territory`

-- (1) An offence committed in an unorganized tract of country in a province, or on a lake, river or other water in it, not included in a territorial division or a provisional judicial district,
-- may be prosecuted in any territorial division or provisional judicial district of that province. "Of the province": the grant is limited to the province's own divisions.
-- src:8653 | Offence in unorganized territory
-- src:8654 | 480 (1) Where an offence is committed in an unorganized tract of country in any province or on a lake, river or other water therein, not included in a territorial division or in a provisional judicial district, proceedings in respect thereof may be commenced and an accused may be charged, tried and punished in respect thereof within any territorial division or provisional judicial district of the province in the same manner as if the offence had been committed within that territorial division or provisional judicial district.
@ref s 480(1) (src:8653-8654)
GIVEN `the offence is committed in an unorganized tract of country in a province, or on a lake, river or other water therein, not included in a territorial division or in a provisional judicial district` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the province in which the unorganized tract lies` IS A `Province or territory`
      `the province in which the territorial division or provisional judicial district lies` IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 480(1) proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division or provisional judicial district` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is committed in an unorganized tract of country in a province, or on a lake, river or other water therein, not included in a territorial division or in a provisional judicial district` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence is committed in an unorganized tract of country in any province or on a lake, river or other water therein, not included in a territorial division or in a provisional judicial district" (a failed "where" on a power: fork: where-on-power)
        IF `the province in which the territorial division or provisional judicial district lies` EQUALS `the province in which the unorganized tract lies` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within any territorial division or provisional judicial district of the province"

-- (2) Where a provisional judicial district or a new territorial division is constituted in the tract, the jurisdiction continues until appropriate provision is made by law for the administration of criminal justice there.
-- An "until": JUST TRUE until the provision is made, JUST FALSE after (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05, applied by analogy to a continuing jurisdiction).
-- src:8655 | New territorial division
-- src:8656 | (2) Where a provisional judicial district or a new territorial division is constituted in an unorganized tract referred to in subsection (1), the jurisdiction conferred by that subsection continues until appropriate provision is made by law for the administration of criminal justice within the provisional judicial district or new territorial division.
@ref s 480(2) (src:8655-8656)
GIVEN `a provisional judicial district or a new territorial division is constituted in an unorganized tract referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appropriate provision has been made by law for the administration of criminal justice within the provisional judicial district or new territorial division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 480(2) subsection (2) continues the jurisdiction conferred by subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a provisional judicial district or a new territorial division is constituted in an unorganized tract referred to in subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a provisional judicial district or a new territorial division is constituted in an unorganized tract referred to in subsection (1)" (a failed "where")
        IF `appropriate provision has been made by law for the administration of criminal justice within the provisional judicial district or new territorial division` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "continues until appropriate provision is made by law for the administration of criminal justice" (an "until" that has passed: fork: until)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 481 -- Offence not in a province`

-- 481 An offence committed in a part of Canada not in a province: proceedings may be commenced and the accused charged, tried and punished within any territorial division in any province.
-- src:8657 | Offence not in a province
-- src:8658 | 481 Where an offence is committed in a part of Canada not in a province, proceedings in respect thereof may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within any territorial division in any province in the same manner as if that offence had been committed in that territorial division.
@ref s 481 (src:8657-8658)
GIVEN `the offence is committed in a part of Canada not in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the territorial division is in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 481 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is committed in a part of Canada not in a province` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence is committed in a part of Canada not in a province" (a failed "where" on a power: fork: where-on-power)
        IF `the territorial division is in a province` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within any territorial division in any province"

§ `Section 481.1 -- Offence in Canadian waters`

-- 481.1 An offence committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or an area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada: proceedings may, whether or not the accused is in Canada,
-- be commenced and the accused charged, tried and punished within any territorial division in Canada. Whether the accused is in Canada changes nothing, so no input stands for it.
-- src:8659 | Offence in Canadian waters
-- src:8660 | 481.1 Where an offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or any area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada, proceedings in respect thereof may, whether or not the accused is in Canada, be commenced and an accused may be charged, tried and punished within any territorial division in Canada in the same manner as if the offence had been committed in that territorial division.
@ref s 481.1 (src:8659-8660)
GIVEN `the offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or any area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the territorial division is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 481.1 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or any area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or any area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada" (a failed "where" on a power: fork: where-on-power)
        IF `the territorial division is in Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within any territorial division in Canada"

§ `Section 481.2 -- Offence outside Canada`

-- 481.2 "Subject to this or any other Act of Parliament", an act or omission committed outside Canada that is an offence when committed outside Canada under this or any other Act of Parliament may be prosecuted
-- in any territorial division in Canada, whether or not the accused is in Canada. Another provision that limits it is an input; where it applies the grant is limited by its own wording: NOT COVERED (fork: subject-to).
-- src:8661 | Offence outside Canada
-- src:8662 | 481.2 Subject to this or any other Act of Parliament, where an act or omission is committed outside Canada and the act or omission is an offence when committed outside Canada under this or any other Act of Parliament, proceedings in respect of the offence may, whether or not the accused is in Canada, be commenced, and an accused may be charged, tried and punished within any territorial division in Canada in the same manner as if the offence had been committed in that territorial division.
@ref s 481.2 (src:8661-8662)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is an offence when committed outside Canada under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another provision of this or any other Act of Parliament limits the section, by the provisions that limit s 481.2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the territorial division is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 481.2 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the act or omission is committed outside Canada` AND `the act or omission is an offence when committed outside Canada under this or any other Act of Parliament`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an act or omission is committed outside Canada and the act or omission is an offence when committed outside Canada under this or any other Act of Parliament" (a failed "where" on a power: fork: where-on-power)
        IF NOT (`another provision of this or any other Act of Parliament limits the section, by the provisions that limit s 481.2` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this or any other Act of Parliament" (fork: subject-to)
        IF `the territorial division is in Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within any territorial division in Canada"

§ `Section 481.3 -- Appearance of accused at trial`

-- 481.3 For greater certainty, the provisions of this Act relating to (a) the requirement of the appearance of an accused at proceedings, and (b) the exceptions to that requirement apply to proceedings
-- commenced in any territorial division pursuant to section 481, 481.1 or 481.2. The section under which the proceedings were commenced is a Provision of the Code (a section number, as a decimal).
-- src:8663 | Appearance of accused at trial
-- src:8664 | 481.3 For greater certainty, the provisions of this Act relating to
-- src:8665 | (a) the requirement of the appearance of an accused at proceedings, and
-- src:8666 | (b) the exceptions to that requirement
-- src:8667 | apply to proceedings commenced in any territorial division pursuant to section 481, 481.1 or 481.2.
@ref s 481.3 (src:8663-8667)
DECLARE `s 481.3 the matter the provisions relate to` IS ONE OF
    `s 481.3(a) the requirement of the appearance of an accused at proceedings`
    `s 481.3(b) the exceptions to the requirement of the appearance of an accused`
    `s 481.3 another matter`

@ref s 481.3 (src:8663-8667)
GIVEN `the section under which the proceedings were commenced in the territorial division` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      matter IS A `s 481.3 the matter the provisions relate to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 481.3 the provisions of this Act relating to the matter apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `the section under which the proceedings were commenced in the territorial division`'s `section` EQUALS 481
                OR `the section under which the proceedings were commenced in the territorial division`'s `section` EQUALS 481.1
                OR `the section under which the proceedings were commenced in the territorial division`'s `section` EQUALS 481.2) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings commenced in any territorial division pursuant to section 481, 481.1 or 481.2"
        IF matter EQUALS `s 481.3 another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section names two matters, the requirement of the appearance of an accused and the exceptions to it, and says nothing of any other
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
